Fix wrong APHY register addresses in suspend.c

The vc4-suspend register map has two addresses swapped relative to
upstream librerpi/common/broadcom/bcm2708_chip/sdc_addr_front.h:

    Symbol                              suspend.c   upstream
    APHY_CSR_PHY_BIST_CNTRL_SPR         0x7EE06020  0x7ee06080
    APHY_CSR_GLBL_ADDR_DLL_LOCK_STAT    0x7EE06010  0x7ee06020

The real 0x7EE06010 is APHY_CSR_GLBL_ADDR_DLL_PH_LD_VAL (phase load
value); the real 0x7EE06020 is the address DLL lock status register.
Author appears to have confused the two.

Effect on suspend/resume:
 - Writing 0x30 to what suspend.c calls PHY_BIST_CNTRL_SPR wrote to
   the DLL lock stat register instead. SDC never told "I'm about to
   change address lines".
 - Reading the "lock stat" as == 3 polled the PH_LD_VAL register.
   Real DLL lock never observed -> 200000-tick timeout every time ->
   "Address DLL lock timeout" -> SDRAM controller restart fails ->
   "FATAL: SDRAM controller failed to come up!" -> watchdog reset.

Symptoms on first-light: after wake IRQ handled, the resume path in
sdram_exit_selfrefresh() gets through DDR PLL re-lock and DPHY DLL
lock, but times out waiting for address DLL lock, then fails to
restart the SDRAM controller, then the watchdog resets the board.

Fix: update both addresses to match upstream. No other code changes
needed; the fix is purely in the address constants.

Apply against pristine vc4-suspend src/ (with `git apply
--ignore-whitespace` if line endings differ).

diff --git a/src/suspend.c b/src/suspend.c
index 1d95642..7c17bf5 100644
--- a/src/suspend.c
+++ b/src/suspend.c
@@ -232,10 +232,14 @@
 #define APHY_CSR_DDR_PLL_MDIV_VALUE      REG32(0x7EE06034)
 #define APHY_CSR_DDR_PLL_LOCK_STATUS     REG32(0x7EE06048)
 #define APHY_CSR_DDR_PLL_PWRDWN          REG32(0x7EE06058)
-/* PHY BIST control -- upstream reset_phy_dll() uses this to signal SDC */
-#define APHY_CSR_PHY_BIST_CNTRL_SPR      REG32(0x7EE06020)
-/* Address DLL lock status -- upstream waits for == 3 */
-#define APHY_CSR_GLBL_ADDR_DLL_LOCK_STAT REG32(0x7EE06010)
+/* PHY BIST control -- upstream reset_phy_dll() uses this to signal SDC.
+ * Per upstream sdc_addr_front.h @ 0x7ee06080; prior value 0x7EE06020 was
+ * actually the address DLL lock status register (see below). */
+#define APHY_CSR_PHY_BIST_CNTRL_SPR      REG32(0x7EE06080)
+/* Address DLL lock status -- upstream waits for == 3.
+ * Per upstream sdc_addr_front.h @ 0x7ee06020; prior value 0x7EE06010 was
+ * actually APHY_CSR_GLBL_ADDR_DLL_PH_LD_VAL (phase load value). */
+#define APHY_CSR_GLBL_ADDR_DLL_LOCK_STAT REG32(0x7EE06020)
 /* Address pad drive/slew -- upstream sdc_addr_front.h: 0x7ee06068 */
 #define APHY_CSR_ADDR_PAD_DRV_SLEW_CTRL  REG32(0x7EE06068)
 /* PVT compensation (process/voltage/temperature recalibration) */
